# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# What the assembly of the loop over frames assumes of the text that the
# builder emits (#302) on a GPU, in double and mixed precision: the text of
# the loop and the stack of the entry at the boundary, to the byte, as
# python-frames-loop.test has them; the memory of the host is read there.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide loop GPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide loop GPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="GPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of the whole potential: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of the dependent terms: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of a program with a barostat: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the loop over frames of a triclinic cell: {{.*}}; in it 0 allocations of the stack, 0 calls in the generic form, 0 arguments of the entry that a frame replaces; {{[0-9]+}} allocations of the stack before it: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the stack of the entry of the whole potential at the boundary after frames 1, 101, and 201: {{[0-9]+}} bytes, then +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: the stack of the entry of the dependent terms at the boundary after frames 1, 101, and 201: {{[0-9]+}} bytes, then +0 and +0 bytes (bound 0): True
# CHECK: loop passed
